00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:58.550
Of course, the best way
to deal with mistakes is

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.510
to avoid them in the first place.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:03.690
So now let me share a couple
of tips and strategies

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.610
that you can use to avoid

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.500
or at least decrease the
numbers of mistakes that you do.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.550
The first is to work with checklists.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.390
So whenever you do a task repeatedly

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.970
and this task is prone to errors,

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:17.950
use a checklist with all the things

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.100
that you want to regularly check

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.230
before you hand in the deliverable.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:25.010
In professional services
jobs, like consulting,

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:28.290
one thing where this for sure
will be helpful are documents.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:32.090
In the beginning of my career
I often did minor mistakes

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.450
in my documents

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.660
and for that I created a checklist

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:37.210
that I always went through,

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:38.560
that I always checked

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:41.740
before I actually sent
and distributed a document

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.210
to colleagues or to clients.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.870
So if you're interested in
this checklist that I used,

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.400
you can actually download it.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.920
I will include a download link

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.690
below in the video description.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:52.140
So I polished it a little bit,

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:52.973
but at its core,

00:12:52.973 --> 00:12:54.960
it's really the checklist that I used

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.730
while I worked at McKinsey.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:59.580
So I hope several of you
will find it helpful as well.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:01.690
Feel free to download
it for free, of course,

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:03.340
via the link in the video description.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:07.280
Another tactic that you could
and should use are check sums

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:10.120
and plausibility checks
in your Excel models.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.110
So as a consultant,

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:13.330
you will very frequently work with models.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:16.543
Often, also write complex
and large financial models.

00:13:16.543 --> 00:13:20.000
Here it's very important
to include maybe one tab

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.340
with different check sums,
different plausibility checks

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:24.990
where you do calculations like,

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:28.680
oh, probably the sum of all
these figures should equal

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.500
this other figure that you
have there in the other tab.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:34.500
You'll do different checks
like that, plausibility checks,

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:35.333
because, of course,

00:13:35.333 --> 00:13:37.720
you will over time frequently
change assumptions,

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.860
change data inputs in such a model.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.130
And sometimes these changes can lead

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.680
to certain elements of the model breaking,

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.460
which you should be able to detect

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:47.470
with techniques like this.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.660
Next tip is to print out documents.

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.150
So surely you here, maybe
people are different,

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:54.530
but I can definitely say, for myself,

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:55.670
and I know that this is true

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:57.660
for many other colleagues as well,

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:01.500
that for me it is always
much easier to spot mistakes

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.730
in documents,

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.860
so let it be grammar or spelling mistakes,

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.490
but also content mistakes,

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.840
things that just do not align,

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.210
do not really fit,

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:11.620
if I have the document printed out,

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.940
compared to just looking
at it on a screen,

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:17.380
maybe even a small screen
on a small notebook.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.550
So whenever possible, especially
for important documents,

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.760
I would recommend you to print them out,

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.460
have them there in front of you,

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:28.810
go over it page by page and
check every single thing.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.160
Read everything,

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.090
just to make sure the document is fine.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.840
And by this, you will likely
spot all the last mistakes.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:36.040
And last but not least,

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:39.240
one technique that is
really highly effective

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:42.370
if you work in a team and you
jointly worked on a document,

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:44.220
is to, before you send it out,

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.960
you sit all together in your team room,

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:49.830
you project the document to the wall,

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:53.870
and then the whole team
looks at every single slide,

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:57.050
every single page for a couple of seconds

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:01.070
and try to spot any errors,
any inconsistencies.

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.360
And then you really go slide by slide

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:06.200
and jointly have a look at it together

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.640
to discuss this and to criticize this.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:10.080
So this, from my experience,

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.410
is really a highly effective measure.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.990
Of course, you could
just send it to everyone,

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:16.260
and tell everyone, "Oh,
please read it yourself.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:17.580
Spot the mistakes."

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.250
But then, like, not everyone
will do this very diligently.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.810
If you have everyone together
and just 100% focused

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.570
on reviewing the document,

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:28.730
here the chances are quite
high that you will really find

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:31.880
even the most minor
problems on the slides.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:34.210
So of course there will
be many other techniques

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:35.860
that you could apply as well.

